-# Canonical Kronk auth-form shell. Used by every Devise view that
-# takes a form on a Rails-served page: sign-in, forgot password,
-# reset password, resend confirmation, email setup — and also by the
-# ambient landing at `/` (home#landing), so every signed-out surface
-# reads as the same page.
-#
-# Renders (top → bottom):
-#   * Hero wordmark (`ЖЯѺƝ₭`, big and centred) — always.
-#   * Optional H2 title (per-flow: "Reset password", "Set a new
-#     password", "Resend confirmation" …). Landing / sign-in skip
-#     this because the wordmark alone reads as the title.
-#   * Optional lede — landing/sign-in uses the community tagline;
-#     other flows use it for the descriptive sub-headline.
-#   * The form body (yielded as a block).
-#   * Optional footer links via `_links.html.haml` (context-aware —
-#     shows Login/Register/Forgot/Confirmation/About/How-it-works
-#     as appropriate).
-#
-# Locals:
-#   title:        (optional) H2 text below the wordmark. Was required
-#                 pre-unification; now optional because landing/sign-in
-#                 lean on the wordmark alone.
-#   lede:         (optional) sub-headline. HAML string, may include
-#                 links.
-#   footer_links: (optional, default true) render `_links.html.haml`
-#                 below the form.

:ruby
  title        = local_assigns[:title]
  lede         = local_assigns[:lede]
  footer_links = local_assigns.fetch(:footer_links, true)

.kronk-auth-shell
  %header.kronk-auth-shell__header
    %h1.kronk-auth-shell__hero
      = render 'shared/kronk_wordmark', size: :hero
      %span.sr-only= t('kronk.landing.wordmark_sr_label')
    - if title
      %h2.kronk-auth-shell__title= title
    - if lede
      %p.kronk-auth-shell__lede= lede

  .kronk-auth-shell__body
    = yield

  - if footer_links
    .kronk-auth-shell__footer
      = render 'auth/shared/links'
